DMA chains: the tag limit is only a guard against a chain that loops forever (4096 -> 1 << 20).

What it fixes: the DMAC chain walker stopped after 4096 tags and treated the chain as done. A normal fight frame
of this game sends a VIF1 chain of about 3,700 tags; a busy one goes past 4096 (four fighters and Luffy's special
move on the Hidden Leaf stage: 4096 from the hit on, every frame). The tags after the 4096th were dropped, and with
them the end of the frame: its last draws and its last MSKPATH3 liftings. The GIF channel's texture uploads, held by
the mask and released one packet per lifting (patch 0042), then stayed queued and reached the GS one or more frames
late, so stage, fighters and HUD were drawn with other textures (the "garbage after the special move" reports; any
character or stage with enough on screen can hit it). The console has no such limit.
Now: 1 << 20 tags, still a stop for a corrupt chain that loops. Same for every channel that walks chains.
Verified: tools/run/scripts/konoha_ougi.txt with P1 = Luffy (Right x3 before the character Circle) on Windows,
Vulkan and software renderers, 1x and 5x: the special move and the stage draw correctly; before, from blank ~6653
on, the GIF chain had 79-80 packets and the VIF1 chain 53 liftings, ending masked (docs/journal/069).

diff --git a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
--- a/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
+++ b/ps2xRuntime/src/lib/ps2_memory.cpp
@@ -1386,7 +1386,10 @@
                     uint32_t asr1 = m_ioRegisters[channelBase + 0x50];
                     uint32_t asp = (chcr >> 4) & 0x3u;
                     const bool tieEnabled = (chcr & (1u << 7)) != 0u;
-                    const int kMaxChainTags = 4096;
+                    // Only a guard against a chain that loops forever: the console has no limit, and a busy frame of
+                    // this game's VIF1 chain goes past 4096 tags (Luffy's special move: the end of the frame, with
+                    // its last PATH3 releases and draws, was cut off and the textures went out of step).
+                    const int kMaxChainTags = 1 << 20;
                     std::vector<uint8_t> chainBuf = acquireChainBuffer();
 
                     auto appendData = [&](uint32_t srcAddr, uint32_t qwCount)
